<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office over the Friday-to-Sunday weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc.</p>
<p>Final data are due Monday. (Rank last week in parentheses)</p>
<p>    1 (1) Star Wars ....................... $22.8 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Dante's Peak .....................$18.6 million</p>
<p>    3 (*) The Beautician and the Beast ..... $4.0 million</p>
<p>    4 (2) Jerry Maguire .................... $3.6 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) Scream ........................... $3.5 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) Evita ............................ $3.0 million</p>
<p>    7 (5) Metro ............................ $2.4 million</p>
<p>    8(14) The English Patient .............. $2.2 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) Beverly Hills Ninja .............. $2.1 million</p>
<p>    10 (7) In Love and War .................. $1.9 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Star Wars&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;The Beautician and the Beast&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; and &quot;Beverly Hills Ninja&quot; are released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; and &quot;The English Patient&quot; are released by Miramax Films, a unit of Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Metro&quot; and &quot;Evita&quot; are released by Disney.</p>
<p>&quot;In Love and War&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
